    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_battle_00",
      "value": "To attack, select the soldier who will make the charge. If an enemy is within range, on a green tile, simply select the enemy soldier to begin the attack."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.speaker.blue_king",
      "value": "Blue King"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_battle_01",
      "value": "But remember: in battle, strength determines the winner. The soldier with the higher strength wins the fight."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_bomb_00",
      "value": "Hidden among the enemy soldiers are traps: extremely dangerous bombs capable of destroying almost any soldier in our army."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_bomb_01",
      "value": "Fortunately, we have an engineer who specializes in defusing them. Use him whenever you suspect an enemy piece might be a bomb."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_firsttimeplaying_00",
      "value": "Hello, and welcome to Kings of Antikva. I see this is your first time here. Come, I'll show you everything you need to know."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_force_00",
      "value": "Each soldier has a strength level. You can see this value below each one. Strength ranges from 1 to 9, with 9 being the highest level."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_gotogame_00",
      "value": "I think you're ready to put your knowledge into practice. Let's run a quick simulation and see what you've learned."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_intro_00",
      "value": "Hello, Commander. Allow me to introduce myself. I am the one and only true King of Antikva."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_intro_01",
      "value": "That's a lie! I am the true King of Antikva!"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.speaker.red_king",
      "value": "Red King"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_intro_02",
      "value": "NO, I AM!"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_intro_03",
      "value": "NO, I AM!"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_intro_04",
      "value": "As you can see, I need your help to defeat this impostor and reclaim my throne as the one and only true King of Antikva."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_intro_05",
      "value": "I will fight alongside my men on the front lines, so I need you to command my troops. Come, I'll show you how."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_killer_00",
      "value": "The enemy King is just as powerful as I am. That's why I trained a special soldier capable of defeating him."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_killer_01",
      "value": "However, he was trained solely for that mission and is not as effective against other soldiers. Use him carefully, and attack only when you are certain you have found the enemy King."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_objective_00",
      "value": "The armies are hidden by a fog of war, preventing us from knowing which soldier is which on the enemy side. The advantage is that they cannot see our soldiers either. You will see your own army normally, but the enemy soldiers will remain hidden."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_objective_01",
      "value": "To win this war, we need to find the enemy's treasure, which is hidden somewhere among his army."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_position_00",
      "value": "Let's start by deploying our army. Arrange the soldiers however you like, but remember: protect my treasure at all costs!!!!!"
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_timer_00",
      "value": "Here you can see whose turn it is and how much time remains before the next turn. Keep an eye on the timer: if we take too long, the enemy will seize the initiative and advance against us."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_walk_normal_00",
      "value": "Let's start with the basics. To move a soldier, click on it and then choose one of the available tiles. The tiles it can move to will appear in green on the board."
    },
    {
      "key": "dialogue.dialogue_walk_soldier_00",
      "value": "Basic soldiers can move more than one tile per turn. Use this range wisely to advance more quickly toward the enemy's treasure."
    },
